 "summary": "Query language of the Fauna distributed document-relational database. FQL v4 was an S-expression-like functional API embedded in host-language drivers; FQL v10 (2023) is a TypeScript-inspired language with method chaining over sets (Collection.where(...).order(...).map(...)), projection, user-defined functions and optional static type checking.",
 "status": "historical",
 "defined_by": [
  "vendor-specification",
  "reference-implementation"
 ],
 "homepage": "https://github.com/fauna/faunadb",
 "influenced_by": [
  "typescript"
 ],
 "level_notes": {
  "1": "The vendor reference (docs.fauna.com) is no longer reachable after the Fauna service shut down in 2025; no level-1 document could be linked. The open-sourced server README describes FQL and Fauna Schema Language.",
  "0": "Fauna open-sourced its database core (fauna/faunadb, Scala): FQL v10 lexer/parser, AST, a type checker with structural/gradual types, and the interpreter and standard library. Official drivers (fauna-js, fauna-go, fauna-dotnet) show the wire protocol and query composition.",
  "3": "No Wikipedia article for Fauna; PLDB's 'fql' is an unrelated language."
 },
